IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`

-- ind-a-tests-commencement.l4: independent tests of the commencement of Articles 1 to 12 (SC-01 to SC-04 of WORK/ind-a/expectations.md).
-- Convention C1: a provision is in force on day D iff D is on or after its commencement day. Parts 1 to 3 (Articles 1 to 7): 21 November 2014; Part 4 (Articles 8 to 12): 1 May 2018.
-- The groups G1 to G4 do not gate on commencement; G7's resolver answers it, so these tests ask G7 about Articles 1 to 12.

§ `ind-a tests: commencement of Articles 1 to 12`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a Article in force` n d MEANS `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`an Article of the Law as now numbered` n) d `the favoured interpretation`

-- SC-01 Articles 1 to 7: not in force on 2014-11-20; in force on 2014-11-21 (src:876-877)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Article in force` 1 (YMD 2014 11 20)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Article in force` 2 (YMD 2014 11 20)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Article in force` 5 (YMD 2014 11 20)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a Article in force` 7 (YMD 2014 11 20)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 1 (YMD 2014 11 21)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 2 (YMD 2014 11 21)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 3 (YMD 2014 11 21)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 4 (YMD 2014 11 21)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 5 (YMD 2014 11 21)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 6 (YMD 2014 11 21)
#ASSERT `ind-a Article in force` 7 (YMD 2014 11 21)
